<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kiram-Bates Treaty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Bates Treaty, Kiram–Bates Treaty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kiram-Bates Treaty was an agreement signed in August 1899 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, represented by General John C. Bates, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamalul-kiram-ii">Jamalul Kiram II</a> of Sulu. It recognised American <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> while promising non-interference in the sultanate's internal affairs and religion, keeping the Sulu Muslims neutral during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a>. The United States abrogated it unilaterally in 1904, after it had set up the Moro Province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kiram-bates-treaty.jpg" alt="Kiram-Bates Treaty" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miscellaneous Items in High Demand, PPOC, Library of Congress · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Major_Hugh_Scott,_Military_Governor_of_the_Sulu_Archipelago,_Philippines,_Sultan_Jamalul_Kiram_II,_interpreter_Charles_Schuck,_and_local_government_officials_and_hadjis,_dressed_to_call_on_LCCN2016650207.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
